# =====================================================================
# mva-research .gitignore
# PRIVACY-CRITICAL FILE. Philosophy: DENY BY DEFAULT for anything that
# could carry patient-derived genomic or clinical data.
#
# Git rule that constrains this file: you CANNOT re-include a file if
# any PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded. Therefore all genomic denials below
# are FILE-PATTERN denials (never bare directory denials), so that the
# narrow synthetic-fixture negations at the bottom can take effect.
# See docs/privacy-model.md.
# =====================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Sensitive workspace roots (patient data must live OUTSIDE the repo)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
workspace/
/workspace
work/
.work/
private/
sensitive/
patient/
case_data/
real-case/
runs/
out/
output/
results/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Variant call formats
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.vcf.bgz
*.gvcf
*.gvcf.gz
*.g.vcf
*.g.vcf.gz
*.bcf
*.bcf.gz
*.tbi
*.csi
*.idx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Alignment formats
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bam
*.bai
*.cram
*.crai
*.sam
*.sam.gz
*.sai

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Raw reads
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.fastq
*.fq
*.fastq.gz
*.fq.gz
*.fastq.bz2
*.fq.bz2
*.ubam
*.sra
*.bcl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Reference / interval / array / pedigree / clinical
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.fa
*.fasta
*.fa.gz
*.fasta.gz
*.fai
*.2bit
*.dict
*.gtf
*.gtf.gz
*.gff
*.gff3
*.ped
*.fam
*.bim
*.bed
*.pgen
*.psam
*.pvar
*.cnv
*.seg
*.idat
*.gtc
*.phenopacket.json
*.mrn
*.phi
# Tabular formats are denied by default: variant tables, phenotype exports and
# submission CSVs all use them. Narrow negations at the bottom re-admit the
# handful of public/synthetic tables that legitimately live in the repo.
*.tsv
*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Derived analytical artifacts (may contain genotypes)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.parquet
*.feather
*.arrow
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.npz
*.pkl
*.pickle

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. Secrets & credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
# Deliberately NO negation for .env.example: re-including it would re-open the
# `.env.*` deny rule, and `cp .env .env.example` is a one-keystroke mistake away
# from committing real credentials. An example file must be named `env.example`
# (no leading dot), which no deny rule above matches.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.keystore
credentials.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
.netrc
.htpasswd

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. Logs, temp, crash dumps (may echo records)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
*.log.*
crash*.txt
core
core.*
*.stackdump
*.dmp
.tmp/
tmp/
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.snakemake/
.snakemake_timestamp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. Notebooks (outputs can embed patient records)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. Python / tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.venv/
venv/
env/
.eggs/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytype/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.tox/
.nox/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 11. macOS / editor / cloud-sync detritus
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.TemporaryItems
.DocumentRevisions-V100
*.icloud
.dropbox
.dropbox.attr
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/

# =====================================================================
# 12. NARROW NEGATIONS — synthetic, non-patient fixtures ONLY
#
# Every path below is asserted to be fully synthetic. The privacy audit
# re-validates these files on every run (check: synthetic_fixture_scan).
# NEVER add a negation outside tests/fixtures/synthetic/ or
# knowledge/public/.
# =====================================================================
# Re-include the directory levels first. Git never descends into an excluded
# directory, so a file negation is dead unless every parent is re-included.
# (None of the rules above exclude these directories, but the explicit
# re-inclusion makes the intent robust against future edits.)
!tests/
!tests/**/
!knowledge/
!knowledge/**/
!config/
!config/**/
!templates/
!templates/**/

# Synthetic fixtures. Every file matched here is additionally required by the
# privacy audit (check: synthetic_fixtures_marked) to carry the marker
# `##mva_synthetic=true` (or a SYNTH- prefixed sample ID), so a real VCF
# accidentally dropped into this directory FAILS the audit instead of sliding in.
!tests/fixtures/synthetic/**/*.vcf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLIC REFERENCE SLICES (ADR 0012) — a DIFFERENT category from synthetic.
#
# These are real records cut verbatim from public reference releases, so they
# CANNOT honestly carry the ##mva_synthetic=true marker the rules above require,
# and they deliberately do not share that exemption's code path.
#
# What makes them safe is not their provenance but a property of their bytes:
# they are SITES-ONLY. No sample columns, no genotypes, no individual to
# disclose. The privacy audit re-checks that mechanically on every run
# (privacy.audit.vcf_declares_sample_columns, which fails closed), so a file
# here that ever gains a genotype column loses the exemption by itself rather
# than by anyone remembering to look.
#
# Each is regenerated by the make_fixture.py beside it, from a release pinned in
# knowledge/manifests/resources.yaml.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
!tests/fixtures/clinvar/**/*.vcf.gz
!tests/fixtures/clinvar/**/*.vcf.gz.tbi
!tests/fixtures/gnomad/**/*.vcf.bgz
!tests/fixtures/gnomad/**/*.tbi
!tests/fixtures/mane/MANE.*.gtf.gz
!tests/fixtures/mane/MANE.*.summary.txt.gz

!tests/fixtures/synthetic/**/*.ped
!tests/fixtures/synthetic/**/*.fa
!tests/fixtures/synthetic/**/*.fai
!tests/fixtures/synthetic/**/*.bed
!tests/fixtures/synthetic/**/*.tsv
!tests/fixtures/synthetic/**/*.csv
!tests/fixtures/synthetic/**/*.txt

# Public knowledge tables (curated from public databases; no patient content).
!knowledge/public/**/*.tsv
!knowledge/public/**/*.csv
!knowledge/manifests/**/*.tsv

# Literature-derived tables (ADR 0022): rows cited to a PMID, no patient content.
# These carry the Track 2 scientific case and tests/unit/test_track2_bub1b.py reads
# them directly, so a clone without them is a clone whose test suite fails. They get
# NO content-scan softening -- knowledge/literature/ is deliberately absent from
# CONTENT_ALLOWLIST_PREFIXES, so the audit reads every byte of them on its own terms.
!knowledge/literature/**/*.tsv
!knowledge/literature/**/*.csv

# Real public-database derivatives (gnomAD constraint, ClinGen validity, HPO
# gene-to-phenotype) and the MVA disease panel. Public sources, no patient
# content, every file carrying its provenance header. tests/unit/test_knowledge_tables.py
# asserts against these as COMMITTED files, so a clone without them is a clone
# with 14 failing tests and a sources doc pointing at a panel that isn't there.
!knowledge/real/**/*.tsv
!knowledge/disease/**/*.tsv

# Configuration and report templates.
!config/**/*.csv
!config/**/*.tsv
!templates/**/*.csv

# Demo outputs are written to an external workspace, never committed.
demo-workspace/
.demo/

# Golden expectation locks (synthetic-derived, public by construction).
!tests/golden/**/*.csv
!tests/golden/**/*.tsv
!tests/golden/**/*.txt

# Local-only teaching artifact. Not part of the deliverable.
explainer/

# Agent/skill tooling. Local authoring aids, not part of the deliverable.
.agents/
.claude/
skills-lock.json

# Production notes for the Track 2 video. The submitted artifact is the video
# itself; the script that produced it is working material, not a deliverable.
docs/track2-video-script.md
